A||N||7||Formula88||Chime box goes crazy - Film at 11!||||5||
Z||000000||Formula88||03-15-2001||11:32 AM||||Ok, I get in my car this morning to head for work, and the seat belt chime is going off. It hasn't before, but that's cool.  I put my seatbelt on and the dash light goes out, but the chime keeps chiming.  No matter what- shut off the car, start it back, re-close all the doors, etc.  The chime just keeps going continuously.  Easy enough, unplug the chime, but I would like to fix it rather than disable it.  Does the Fiero have just one chime for everything, or are there different sounds for different things.  That could help narrow down the culprit.||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||03-15-2001||11:53 AM||||Yes...one chime box for everything.<P>In Ogre's cave there is a section on how to fix it. Or just visit the boneyard and get another.<P>Would be useful to know whether these are standard issue...whether they come on other cars. I would assume they do.||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||03-15-2001||02:22 PM||||My 85's did that until the chime like burned out or something, i put my 84's in and it contiunes to do it... i wonder what is wrong (i just took it out)<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||03-15-2001||03:35 PM||||I hate those things.  I call it the bonging device.  Mine went off all the time because the emergency brake switch is messed up, and the light is on all the time.  So I pulled it.  solved that problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||03-15-2001||04:15 PM||||Um... Is it going, bing.....bing......bing.....bing<P><B>Or</B> bing.bing.bing.bing.bing.bing.<P>Trying to simulate elapsed time between bings.<BR>The seat belt chime stops after a few seconds even without latching the seat belt.  The one for the emergency brake on the other hand will drive you nuts until the sensor on the lever is released or unplugged.  The same warning chime used for the e-brake is also used for the lights being on with the ignition off too.||||reg||4
Z||000005||Formula88||03-15-2001||04:25 PM||||If that's the case, then it sounds like the emergency brake switch is faulty.  Yea, more stuff to work on my Fiero this weekend!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||03-15-2001||05:03 PM||||John - <BR>we can swap mine for yours this weekend and see if it's the chime unit that's faulty or your parking brake switch.<P>I've never had a PB switch go bad before...||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||03-15-2001||07:16 PM||||Read the chime article in my cave. It will help you determine for certain which line is acting up. It tells you how to get the individual terminals out of the socket w/o damage. Also tells you how to fix a manufacturing defect in the version 2 boxes.||||reg||1
